※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 3024 LANG_IF_ELSE_IS_LAST

※ `else` is the arm that runs when none of the others did, so nothing can be
※ asked after it: an `elif` written there could never be reached.

let n: mut u8 = 3u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u6 { if n < 4u8 { return 2u6 } else { return 3u6 } elif n = 1u8 { return 4u6 } }
